window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b245-344e10586c3b5101.json"]={sha256:"344e10586c3b5101e6a7288b711a4924558f5640760246aaa0fabe0fe0975e4c",value:{"id":"b245","title":"滑雪跳台式消能工","titleEn":"Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以追蹤挑流軌跡入水動量與岩床沖蝕邊界為主線，先用挑流彈道與落點與落差與飛行時間界定水力與構造條件，再將射流功率與承受區、入水動量與方向連結到福祿尺度與表面張力。彈道忽略空氣阻力且以自由射流示意，水墊與岩床反應須另外驗證。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops tracing flip-bucket trajectories impact momentum and rock-scour boundaries through Jet trajectory and landing point and Drop height and flight time, then connects Jet power and receiving zone and Impact momentum and direction to Froude scaling and surface tension. Ballistic examples neglect air resistance and describe free jets; plunge-pool and rock responses require separate verification. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["挑流彈道與落點","Jet trajectory and landing point"],["鼻坎曲率與壓力","Bucket curvature and pressure"],["射流功率與承受區","Jet power and receiving zone"],["入水動量與方向","Impact momentum and direction"],["福祿尺度與表面張力","Froude scaling and surface tension"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["挑流彈道與落點","鼻坎曲率與壓力","射流功率與承受區","入水動量與方向","福祿尺度與表面張力"],"labelsEn":["Jet trajectory and landing point","Bucket curvature and pressure","Jet power and receiving zone","Impact momentum and direction","Froude scaling and surface tension"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查挑流彈道與落點：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m；再獨立檢查落差與飛行時間：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。敏感度：同高起落且挑角30度時，出口速度由20增至25m/s，理想射程由35.31增至55.17m，增加56.25%；射程隨速度平方變化但不代表沖刷深度同倍增加。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。彈道忽略空氣阻力且以自由射流示意，水墊與岩床反應須另外驗證。 將以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Jet trajectory and landing point: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m. Independently examine Drop height and flight time: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s. Sensitivity: at equal launch and landing elevation and a30-degree angle, increasing exit velocity from20 to25m/s raises ideal range from35.31 to55.17m, a56.25 percent increase. Range scales with velocity squared, whereas scour depth does not follow the same rule. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Ballistic examples neglect air resistance and describe free jets; plunge-pool and rock responses require separate verification. Use the following independent check: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b245-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「挑流彈道與落點」與「落差與飛行時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Jet trajectory and landing point\" and \"Drop height and flight time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b245-v15-01","title":"挑流彈道與落點：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Jet trajectory and landing point: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「挑流彈道與落點」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jet trajectory and landing point” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"挑流鼻坎把高速水舌拋向下游水墊，落點受出口速度、角度與落差控制。忽略阻力的質點彈道只估中心線，實際水舌會展寬、破碎與含氣；必須確認使用的是水舌離坎速度而非上游平均速度，且不能把單一落點當成整個沖擊區。 驗證時應由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程，並辨識以下失效情境：把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「挑流彈道與落點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A flip bucket throws a high-speed jet toward a downstream pool. Velocity, angle and elevation difference determine the ideal trajectory. A drag-free particle model estimates a centerline, while real jets spread, fragment and aerate; use launch velocity and distinguish the landing point from the entire impact footprint. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet trajectory and landing point” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「挑流彈道與落點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet trajectory and landing point”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-01-k1","title":"挑流彈道與落點","titleEn":"Jet trajectory and landing point","text":"挑流鼻坎把高速水舌拋向下游水墊，落點受出口速度、角度與落差控制。忽略阻力的質點彈道只估中心線，實際水舌會展寬、破碎與含氣；必須確認使用的是水舌離坎速度而非上游平均速度，且不能把單一落點當成整個沖擊區。","textEn":"A flip bucket throws a high-speed jet toward a downstream pool. Velocity, angle and elevation difference determine the ideal trajectory.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「挑流彈道與落點」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jet trajectory and landing point\" is correct?","options":["理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍","挑流鼻坎把高速水舌拋向下游水墊，落點受出口速度、角度與落差控制。","有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式"],"optionsEn":["The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint","A flip bucket throws a high-speed jet toward a downstream pool.","A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula"],"answer":1,"explanation":"挑流鼻坎把高速水舌拋向下游水墊，落點受出口速度、角度與落差控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A flip bucket throws a high-speed jet toward a downstream pool. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b245-v15-02","title":"挑流彈道與落點：定量估算","titleEn":"Jet trajectory and landing point: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「挑流彈道與落點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jet trajectory and landing point” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「挑流彈道與落點」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jet trajectory and landing point\", which statement holds?","options":["水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能","水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","原創教學假設：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m。"],"optionsEn":["A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket","A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Original teaching assumptions: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Equal launch/landing elevation; V=20 m/s; angle=30 degrees; range=20**2*sin(60 degrees)/9.81=35.3119 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b245-v15-03","title":"挑流彈道與落點：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jet trajectory and landing point: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「挑流彈道與落點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jet trajectory and landing point” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「挑流彈道與落點」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jet trajectory and landing point\"?","options":["由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起"],"optionsEn":["Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts"],"answer":0,"explanation":"由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b245-v15-04","title":"挑流彈道與落點：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jet trajectory and landing point: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「挑流彈道與落點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jet trajectory and landing point” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。診斷時應採取以下查核：由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. Diagnose it by the following check: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。診斷時應採取以下查核：由高速攝影追蹤水舌邊界並核對出口速度與實際尾水高程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. Diagnose it by the following check: Track jet boundaries with high-speed imaging and verify launch velocity and actual tailwater elevation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「挑流彈道與落點」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jet trajectory and landing point\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。","有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region.","A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把高水位尾水仍當同高落點會誤判沖擊位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming equal elevations despite high tailwater misplaces the impact region. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b245-v15-05","title":"落差與飛行時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drop height and flight time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「落差與飛行時間」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drop height and flight time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水舌由較高出口落入低處水面時，垂直運動包含初始向上速度與重力加速，應取二次方程的正時間根。以同高公式代替會低估射程；水位波動與射流破碎使接觸面並非固定平面，仍需量測與模型確認。 驗證時應以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程，並辨識以下失效情境：選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「落差與飛行時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a jet launched above the pool, vertical motion includes initial upward velocity and gravity. Use the positive time root rather than the equal-elevation shortcut, which underestimates range. Pool waves and jet fragmentation make the contact surface variable, so measurements must validate the idealized trajectory. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drop height and flight time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「落差與飛行時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drop height and flight time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-05-k1","title":"落差與飛行時間","titleEn":"Drop height and flight time","text":"水舌由較高出口落入低處水面時，垂直運動包含初始向上速度與重力加速，應取二次方程的正時間根。以同高公式代替會低估射程；水位波動與射流破碎使接觸面並非固定平面，仍需量測與模型確認。","textEn":"For a jet launched above the pool, vertical motion includes initial upward velocity and gravity. Use the positive time root rather than the equal-elevation shortcut, which underestimates range.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「落差與飛行時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drop height and flight time\" is correct?","options":["有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式","鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算","水舌由較高出口落入低處水面時，垂直運動包含初始向上速度與重力加速，應取二次方程的正時間根。"],"optionsEn":["A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula","Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure","For a jet launched above the pool, vertical motion includes initial upward velocity and gravity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水舌由較高出口落入低處水面時，垂直運動包含初始向上速度與重力加速，應取二次方程的正時間根。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a jet launched above the pool, vertical motion includes initial upward velocity and gravity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b245-v15-06","title":"落差與飛行時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Drop height and flight time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「落差與飛行時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drop height and flight time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「落差與飛行時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drop height and flight time\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。","總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度","只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s.","Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth","Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: UpwardVelocity=10 m/s; drop=8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; flightTime=(10+sqrt(10**2+2*9.81*8))/9.81=2.65341 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b245-v15-07","title":"落差與飛行時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drop height and flight time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「落差與飛行時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drop height and flight time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「落差與飛行時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drop height and flight time\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程。","完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation.","Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b245-v15-08","title":"落差與飛行時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drop height and flight time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「落差與飛行時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drop height and flight time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. Diagnose it by the following check: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同步影像核對離坎與入水時刻及水面平均高程，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. Diagnose it by the following check: Use synchronized images to verify launch and impact times and mean pool elevation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「落差與飛行時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drop height and flight time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算","選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure","Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory."],"answer":2,"explanation":"選錯負時間根會產生看似有值但不具物理意義的軌跡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting the negative time root produces a numerical but nonphysical trajectory. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b245-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「鼻坎曲率與壓力」與「速度水頭與能量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bucket curvature and pressure\" and \"Velocity head and jet energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b245-v15-09","title":"鼻坎曲率與壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bucket curvature and pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「鼻坎曲率與壓力」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bucket curvature and pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曲面使水流向上轉彎，需要向心加速度，底部壓力因此不只由靜水深決定。薄層近似可估曲率附加壓力，但水深與速度沿坎面並不一定均勻；過渡曲率突變還可能造成局部分離，須檢查沿程壓力而非只有出口角度。 驗證時應沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照，並辨識以下失效情境：曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鼻坎曲率與壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Turning flow upward requires centripetal acceleration, so bucket pressure is not purely hydrostatic. A thin-layer approximation estimates added curvature pressure, but depth and velocity vary along the surface. Abrupt curvature transitions can produce separation; examine the pressure distribution instead of checking only the launch angle. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bucket curvature and pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000).","failure":"常見誤解：「鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鼻坎曲率與壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bucket curvature and pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-09-k1","title":"鼻坎曲率與壓力","titleEn":"Bucket curvature and pressure","text":"曲面使水流向上轉彎，需要向心加速度，底部壓力因此不只由靜水深決定。薄層近似可估曲率附加壓力，但水深與速度沿坎面並不一定均勻；過渡曲率突變還可能造成局部分離，須檢查沿程壓力而非只有出口角度。","textEn":"Turning flow upward requires centripetal acceleration, so bucket pressure is not purely hydrostatic. A thin-layer approximation estimates added curvature pressure, but depth and velocity vary along the surface.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鼻坎曲率與壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bucket curvature and pressure\" is correct?","options":["曲面使水流向上轉彎，需要向心加速度，底部壓力因此不只由靜水深決定。","鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算","水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能"],"optionsEn":["Turning flow upward requires centripetal acceleration, so bucket pressure is not purely hydrostatic.","Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure","A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket"],"answer":0,"explanation":"曲面使水流向上轉彎，需要向心加速度，底部壓力因此不只由靜水深決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Turning flow upward requires centripetal acceleration, so bucket pressure is not purely hydrostatic. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b245-v15-10","title":"鼻坎曲率與壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Bucket curvature and pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鼻坎曲率與壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bucket curvature and pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000)。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000). These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000)。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000). These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鼻坎曲率與壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bucket curvature and pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000)。","平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起"],"optionsEn":["A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; V=22 m/s; flowDepth=0.8 m; radius=18 m; curvaturePressure=rho*V**2*flowDepth/radius/1000=21.5111 kPa (SI pressure in Pa divided by1000). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b245-v15-11","title":"鼻坎曲率與壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bucket curvature and pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鼻坎曲率與壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bucket curvature and pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鼻坎曲率與壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bucket curvature and pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似","沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration","Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b245-v15-12","title":"鼻坎曲率與壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bucket curvature and pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鼻坎曲率與壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bucket curvature and pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿曲面布設壓力孔並將低壓區與曲率過渡位置對照，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures along the bucket and compare low-pressure regions with curvature transitions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鼻坎曲率與壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bucket curvature and pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能"],"optionsEn":["Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket"],"answer":0,"explanation":"曲率接續不平順可能引發分離與局部氣蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Abrupt curvature transitions can cause separation and local cavitation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b245-v15-13","title":"速度水頭與能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Velocity head and jet energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「速度水頭與能量」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Velocity head and jet energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"離坎水流的速度水頭代表每單位重量所帶動能，挑流只是把能量移到下游空間消散，並未在鼻坎自動消除。出口高程、沿程損失與速度分布共同決定可用能量；要區分水頭、能量與功率，避免量綱混淆。 驗證時應核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭，並辨識以下失效情境：將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「速度水頭與能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Velocity head represents kinetic energy per unit weight. A flip bucket relocates dissipation downstream rather than eliminating energy at the lip. Elevation, approach losses and velocity distribution determine available energy; distinguish head from energy and power so that apparent dissipation is not a dimensional bookkeeping mistake. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Velocity head and jet energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「速度水頭與能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Velocity head and jet energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-13-k1","title":"速度水頭與能量","titleEn":"Velocity head and jet energy","text":"離坎水流的速度水頭代表每單位重量所帶動能，挑流只是把能量移到下游空間消散，並未在鼻坎自動消除。出口高程、沿程損失與速度分布共同決定可用能量；要區分水頭、能量與功率，避免量綱混淆。","textEn":"Velocity head represents kinetic energy per unit weight. A flip bucket relocates dissipation downstream rather than eliminating energy at the lip.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「速度水頭與能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Velocity head and jet energy\" is correct?","options":["水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能","離坎水流的速度水頭代表每單位重量所帶動能，挑流只是把能量移到下游空間消散，並未在鼻坎自動消除。","總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度"],"optionsEn":["A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket","Velocity head represents kinetic energy per unit weight.","Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"離坎水流的速度水頭代表每單位重量所帶動能，挑流只是把能量移到下游空間消散，並未在鼻坎自動消除。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Velocity head represents kinetic energy per unit weight. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b245-v15-14","title":"速度水頭與能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Velocity head and jet energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「速度水頭與能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Velocity head and jet energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「速度水頭與能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Velocity head and jet energy\", which statement holds?","options":["只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同","完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕","原創教學假設：V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m。"],"optionsEn":["Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact","Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed","Original teaching assumptions: V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=24 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; velocityHead=24**2/(2*9.81)=29.3578 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b245-v15-15","title":"速度水頭與能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Velocity head and jet energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「速度水頭與能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Velocity head and jet energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「速度水頭與能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Velocity head and jet energy\"?","options":["核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍"],"optionsEn":["Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b245-v15-16","title":"速度水頭與能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Velocity head and jet energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「速度水頭與能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Velocity head and jet energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. Diagnose it by the following check: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對入口至離坎的能量線並分別列出高程與速度水頭，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. Diagnose it by the following check: Check the energy line to the lip and list elevation and velocity heads separately. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「速度水頭與能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Velocity head and jet energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。","總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact.","Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將射流離開混凝土視為已完全消能會漏掉下游沖擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating departure from concrete as complete dissipation ignores downstream impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b245-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「射流功率與承受區」與「含氣展寬與截面」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Jet power and receiving zone\" and \"Aeration spreading and jet area\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b245-v15-17","title":"射流功率與承受區：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Jet power and receiving zone: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「射流功率與承受區」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jet power and receiving zone” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水力功率將流量與可耗散水頭結合，描述下游需要處理的能量速率。相同功率可由不同流量與速度組合造成，而沖擊、含氣與岩塊拔出機制不同；因此功率只能作系統尺度指標，不能單獨轉成固定的水墊深度。 驗證時應以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布，並辨識以下失效情境：把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「射流功率與承受區」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic power combines discharge and dissipatable head into an energy rate. Equal power can arise from different discharge and velocity combinations with different impact, aeration and rock-block removal behavior. Use power as a system-level indicator rather than converting it directly into a prescribed pool depth. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet power and receiving zone” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「射流功率與承受區」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet power and receiving zone”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-17-k1","title":"射流功率與承受區","titleEn":"Jet power and receiving zone","text":"水力功率將流量與可耗散水頭結合，描述下游需要處理的能量速率。相同功率可由不同流量與速度組合造成，而沖擊、含氣與岩塊拔出機制不同；因此功率只能作系統尺度指標，不能單獨轉成固定的水墊深度。","textEn":"Hydraulic power combines discharge and dissipatable head into an energy rate. Equal power can arise from different discharge and velocity combinations with different impact, aeration and rock-block removal behavior.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「射流功率與承受區」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jet power and receiving zone\" is correct?","options":["總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度","水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","水力功率將流量與可耗散水頭結合，描述下游需要處理的能量速率。"],"optionsEn":["Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth","A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Hydraulic power combines discharge and dissipatable head into an energy rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水力功率將流量與可耗散水頭結合，描述下游需要處理的能量速率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic power combines discharge and dissipatable head into an energy rate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b245-v15-18","title":"射流功率與承受區：定量估算","titleEn":"Jet power and receiving zone: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「射流功率與承受區」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jet power and receiving zone” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「射流功率與承受區」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jet power and receiving zone\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW。","平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起","彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW.","Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts","Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=80 m3/s; H=40 m; power=1000*9.81*80*40/1e6=31.392 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b245-v15-19","title":"射流功率與承受區：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jet power and receiving zone: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「射流功率與承受區」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jet power and receiving zone” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「射流功率與承受區」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jet power and receiving zone\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布。","有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint.","A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b245-v15-20","title":"射流功率與承受區：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jet power and receiving zone: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「射流功率與承受區」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jet power and receiving zone” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. Diagnose it by the following check: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。診斷時應採取以下查核：以流量量測與能量線核對功率並繪製沖擊區分布，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. Diagnose it by the following check: Verify power from measured discharge and energy head and map the receiving footprint. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「射流功率與承受區」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jet power and receiving zone\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把總功率均勻攤到全河床會低估集中沖擊強度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Spreading total power uniformly over the whole bed understates concentrated impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b245-v15-21","title":"含氣展寬與截面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Aeration spreading and jet area: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「含氣展寬與截面」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aeration spreading and jet area” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"空氣捲入會增加水舌混合體積並改變外觀厚度，水量守恆應採液相體積而非混合總體積。均勻含氣率的示意只表達相分率，實際氣泡有滑移與非均勻分布；應同時量測水相流量、混合速度與含氣剖面。 驗證時應以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆，並辨識以下失效情境：將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含氣展寬與截面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Entrained air expands the apparent jet thickness. Liquid continuity uses water volume, not total mixture volume. A uniform void-fraction model illustrates phase accounting, while real bubbles slip and concentrations vary across the jet. Measure liquid flow, mixture velocity and air profiles together before interpreting the visible envelope. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aeration spreading and jet area” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「含氣展寬與截面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aeration spreading and jet area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-21-k1","title":"含氣展寬與截面","titleEn":"Aeration spreading and jet area","text":"空氣捲入會增加水舌混合體積並改變外觀厚度，水量守恆應採液相體積而非混合總體積。均勻含氣率的示意只表達相分率，實際氣泡有滑移與非均勻分布；應同時量測水相流量、混合速度與含氣剖面。","textEn":"Entrained air expands the apparent jet thickness. Liquid continuity uses water volume, not total mixture volume.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「含氣展寬與截面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Aeration spreading and jet area\" is correct?","options":["空氣捲入會增加水舌混合體積並改變外觀厚度，水量守恆應採液相體積而非混合總體積。","水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同"],"optionsEn":["Entrained air expands the apparent jet thickness.","A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空氣捲入會增加水舌混合體積並改變外觀厚度，水量守恆應採液相體積而非混合總體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Entrained air expands the apparent jet thickness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b245-v15-22","title":"含氣展寬與截面：定量估算","titleEn":"Aeration spreading and jet area: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「含氣展寬與截面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aeration spreading and jet area” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「含氣展寬與截面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Aeration spreading and jet area\", which statement holds?","options":["完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕","原創教學假設：LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2。","理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍"],"optionsEn":["Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed","Original teaching assumptions: LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2.","The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: LiquidQ=40 m3/s; uniformAirVoidFraction=0.20; equal phase velocity=20 m/s; mixtureArea=40/((1-0.20)*20)=2.50 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b245-v15-23","title":"含氣展寬與截面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Aeration spreading and jet area: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「含氣展寬與截面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aeration spreading and jet area” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「含氣展寬與截面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Aeration spreading and jet area\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算","以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure","Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b245-v15-24","title":"含氣展寬與截面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Aeration spreading and jet area: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「含氣展寬與截面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aeration spreading and jet area” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以含氣探針與影像量測展寬並核對液相流量守恆，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure spreading with air probes and imaging and check liquid-phase continuity. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「含氣展寬與截面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Aeration spreading and jet area\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同"],"optionsEn":["Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將混合截面全當水會高估液相質量與動量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the entire mixture area as water overstates liquid mass and momentum. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b245-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「入水動量與方向」與「衝擊面積與平均壓力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Impact momentum and direction\" and \"Impact area and average pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b245-v15-25","title":"入水動量與方向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Impact momentum and direction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「入水動量與方向」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Impact momentum and direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"射流入水時的作用取決於速度向量變化，垂直與水平分量對池底與側壁的影響不同。只估完全消除一個分量的平均動量力，不含壓力回授與脈動放大；實際射流可能在水墊中轉向而保留部分動量。 驗證時應以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入水動量與方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Impact depends on vector velocity change, with vertical and horizontal components loading the pool bed and walls differently. A mean force for arresting one component omits pressure feedback and dynamic amplification. A real jet may turn within the pool and retain momentum rather than stopping completely. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Impact momentum and direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入水動量與方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Impact momentum and direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-25-k1","title":"入水動量與方向","titleEn":"Impact momentum and direction","text":"射流入水時的作用取決於速度向量變化，垂直與水平分量對池底與側壁的影響不同。只估完全消除一個分量的平均動量力，不含壓力回授與脈動放大；實際射流可能在水墊中轉向而保留部分動量。","textEn":"Impact depends on vector velocity change, with vertical and horizontal components loading the pool bed and walls differently. A mean force for arresting one component omits pressure feedback and dynamic amplification.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「入水動量與方向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Impact momentum and direction\" is correct?","options":["只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同","射流入水時的作用取決於速度向量變化，垂直與水平分量對池底與側壁的影響不同。","平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起"],"optionsEn":["Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact","Impact depends on vector velocity change, with vertical and horizontal components loading the pool bed and walls differently.","Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"射流入水時的作用取決於速度向量變化，垂直與水平分量對池底與側壁的影響不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Impact depends on vector velocity change, with vertical and horizontal components loading the pool bed and walls differently. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b245-v15-26","title":"入水動量與方向：定量估算","titleEn":"Impact momentum and direction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入水動量與方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Impact momentum and direction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「入水動量與方向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Impact momentum and direction\", which statement holds?","options":["彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似","有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration","A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=30 m3/s; removedVerticalVelocity=18 m/s; meanVerticalForce=1000*30*18/1000=540 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b245-v15-27","title":"入水動量與方向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Impact momentum and direction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入水動量與方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Impact momentum and direction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「入水動量與方向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Impact momentum and direction\"?","options":["以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能"],"optionsEn":["Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b245-v15-28","title":"入水動量與方向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Impact momentum and direction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入水動量與方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Impact momentum and direction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。診斷時應採取以下查核：以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. Diagnose it by the following check: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。診斷時應採取以下查核：以速度剖面與池底壓力積分檢查垂直動量平衡，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. Diagnose it by the following check: Check vertical momentum using velocity profiles and integrated bed pressures. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「入水動量與方向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Impact momentum and direction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。","平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction.","Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略射流轉向後的流出動量會算錯合力方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring outgoing momentum after deflection misstates the resultant force direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b245-v15-29","title":"衝擊面積與平均壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Impact area and average pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「衝擊面積與平均壓力」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Impact area and average pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水墊使射流動量擴散至更大面積，但平均壓力與局部瞬時峰值差異很大。把已知合力除以指定作用面積可示範平均量，不能反推真實壓力分布；池底地形、含氣與射流擺動都可能形成偏心集中區。 驗證時應以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值，並辨識以下失效情境：用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「衝擊面積與平均壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A pool spreads jet momentum over an area, but mean pressure differs greatly from local instantaneous peaks. Dividing a prescribed force by a specified area illustrates only an average and cannot recover the distribution. Bed geometry, aeration and jet oscillation may create eccentric concentrated loading. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Impact area and average pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「衝擊面積與平均壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Impact area and average pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-29-k1","title":"衝擊面積與平均壓力","titleEn":"Impact area and average pressure","text":"水墊使射流動量擴散至更大面積，但平均壓力與局部瞬時峰值差異很大。把已知合力除以指定作用面積可示範平均量，不能反推真實壓力分布；池底地形、含氣與射流擺動都可能形成偏心集中區。","textEn":"A pool spreads jet momentum over an area, but mean pressure differs greatly from local instantaneous peaks. Dividing a prescribed force by a specified area illustrates only an average and cannot recover the distribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「衝擊面積與平均壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Impact area and average pressure\" is correct?","options":["平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起","完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕","水墊使射流動量擴散至更大面積，但平均壓力與局部瞬時峰值差異很大。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts","Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed","A pool spreads jet momentum over an area, but mean pressure differs greatly from local instantaneous peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水墊使射流動量擴散至更大面積，但平均壓力與局部瞬時峰值差異很大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A pool spreads jet momentum over an area, but mean pressure differs greatly from local instantaneous peaks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b245-v15-30","title":"衝擊面積與平均壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Impact area and average pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「衝擊面積與平均壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Impact area and average pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「衝擊面積與平均壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Impact area and average pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa。","理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍","鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa.","The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint","Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedMeanForce=600 kN; effectiveImpactArea=24 m2; meanPressure=600/24=25 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b245-v15-31","title":"衝擊面積與平均壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Impact area and average pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「衝擊面積與平均壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Impact area and average pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「衝擊面積與平均壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Impact area and average pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值。","總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays.","Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b245-v15-32","title":"衝擊面積與平均壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Impact area and average pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「衝擊面積與平均壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Impact area and average pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均壓力低就保證局部岩塊不會被拔起」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean pressure guarantees that no local rock block lifts\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多點同步壓力量測比較面積平均與局部峰值，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare spatially averaged pressure with local peaks using synchronized pressure arrays. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「衝擊面積與平均壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Impact area and average pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕","用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed","Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用全池面積平均會掩蓋水舌落點下的高壓區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging over the whole pool hides high pressure beneath the jet footprint. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b245-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「岩節理揚力與抗力」與「福祿尺度與表面張力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint uplift and rock resistance\" and \"Froude scaling and surface tension\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b245-v15-33","title":"岩節理揚力與抗力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint uplift and rock resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「岩節理揚力與抗力」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint uplift and rock resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"射流脈壓可沿節理傳入岩塊底面，使岩塊自重、浮力與節理抗力之間的平衡改變。簡化水下自重只提供一項抗力，不包含咬合與剪阻；需調查節理連通、開口與塊體尺寸，不能僅用完整岩石抗壓強度預測沖蝕。 驗證時應繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差，並辨識以下失效情境：連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩節理揚力與抗力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Jet pressure can enter joints beneath rock blocks and alter the balance of weight, buoyancy and joint resistance. Submerged weight is only one resisting component and excludes interlock and shear. Investigate joint connectivity, aperture and block geometry; intact compressive strength alone cannot predict plucking or scour. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint uplift and rock resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岩節理揚力與抗力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint uplift and rock resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-33-k1","title":"岩節理揚力與抗力","titleEn":"Joint uplift and rock resistance","text":"射流脈壓可沿節理傳入岩塊底面，使岩塊自重、浮力與節理抗力之間的平衡改變。簡化水下自重只提供一項抗力，不包含咬合與剪阻；需調查節理連通、開口與塊體尺寸，不能僅用完整岩石抗壓強度預測沖蝕。","textEn":"Jet pressure can enter joints beneath rock blocks and alter the balance of weight, buoyancy and joint resistance. Submerged weight is only one resisting component and excludes interlock and shear.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岩節理揚力與抗力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint uplift and rock resistance\" is correct?","options":["射流脈壓可沿節理傳入岩塊底面，使岩塊自重、浮力與節理抗力之間的平衡改變。","完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕","彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似"],"optionsEn":["Jet pressure can enter joints beneath rock blocks and alter the balance of weight, buoyancy and joint resistance.","Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed","Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"射流脈壓可沿節理傳入岩塊底面，使岩塊自重、浮力與節理抗力之間的平衡改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Jet pressure can enter joints beneath rock blocks and alter the balance of weight, buoyancy and joint resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b245-v15-34","title":"岩節理揚力與抗力：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint uplift and rock resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岩節理揚力與抗力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint uplift and rock resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岩節理揚力與抗力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint uplift and rock resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["有落差的挑流仍可沿用同高射程公式","原創教學假設：rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN。","水舌一離開鼻坎就已經失去全部動能"],"optionsEn":["A jet with elevation drop still obeys the equal-elevation range formula","Original teaching assumptions: rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN.","A jet loses all kinetic energy as soon as it leaves the bucket"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rockDensity=2650 kg/m3; waterDensity=1000 kg/m3; volume=2 m3; submergedWeight=(2650-1000)*9.81*2/1000=32.373 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b245-v15-35","title":"岩節理揚力與抗力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint uplift and rock resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岩節理揚力與抗力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint uplift and rock resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岩節理揚力與抗力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint uplift and rock resistance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","水舌外觀變厚就保證液態流量已增加","繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A thicker visible jet guarantees increased liquid discharge","Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b245-v15-36","title":"岩節理揚力與抗力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint uplift and rock resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岩節理揚力與抗力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint uplift and rock resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完整岩石強度高就保證節理岩床不沖蝕」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Strong intact rock guarantees a scour-proof jointed bed\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。診斷時應採取以下查核：繪製節理網與塊體尺寸並同步量測節理內外壓差，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. Diagnose it by the following check: Map joints and block sizes and measure pressure differences across connected joints. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岩節理揚力與抗力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint uplift and rock resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似"],"optionsEn":["Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"連通節理將脈壓送至塊底可能降低有效抗拔餘量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Connected joints transmit pulses beneath blocks and can reduce uplift resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b245-v15-37","title":"福祿尺度與表面張力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Froude scaling and surface tension: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「福祿尺度與表面張力」如何影響滑雪跳台式消能工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Froude scaling and surface tension” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Ski-jump spillway energy dissipation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"挑流模型常以重力相似重現彈道，但細水舌的破碎與含氣受到表面張力影響，韋伯數可提示這種尺度偏差。相同水質的縮尺模型無法同時保持所有無因次數；應把落點驗證與氣泡破碎驗證分開報告。 驗證時應比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點，並辨識以下失效情境：過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「福祿尺度與表面張力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gravity similarity can reproduce trajectories while surface tension changes thin-jet breakup and aeration. Weber number highlights this scale effect. A reduced model using the same water cannot preserve every dimensionless group simultaneously; report trajectory validation separately from bubble and breakup fidelity instead of treating all observations as equally scalable. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Froude scaling and surface tension” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11.","failure":"常見誤解：「彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「福祿尺度與表面張力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Froude scaling and surface tension”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-37-k1","title":"福祿尺度與表面張力","titleEn":"Froude scaling and surface tension","text":"挑流模型常以重力相似重現彈道，但細水舌的破碎與含氣受到表面張力影響，韋伯數可提示這種尺度偏差。相同水質的縮尺模型無法同時保持所有無因次數；應把落點驗證與氣泡破碎驗證分開報告。","textEn":"Gravity similarity can reproduce trajectories while surface tension changes thin-jet breakup and aeration. Weber number highlights this scale effect.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「福祿尺度與表面張力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Froude scaling and surface tension\" is correct?","options":["彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似","挑流模型常以重力相似重現彈道，但細水舌的破碎與含氣受到表面張力影響，韋伯數可提示這種尺度偏差。","理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍"],"optionsEn":["Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration","Gravity similarity can reproduce trajectories while surface tension changes thin-jet breakup and aeration.","The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint"],"answer":1,"explanation":"挑流模型常以重力相似重現彈道，但細水舌的破碎與含氣受到表面張力影響，韋伯數可提示這種尺度偏差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gravity similarity can reproduce trajectories while surface tension changes thin-jet breakup and aeration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b245-v15-38","title":"福祿尺度與表面張力：定量估算","titleEn":"Froude scaling and surface tension: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「福祿尺度與表面張力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Froude scaling and surface tension” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「福祿尺度與表面張力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Froude scaling and surface tension\", which statement holds?","options":["鼻坎壓力只要用靜水深就能完整計算","總水力功率可以單獨決定所需水墊深度","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11。"],"optionsEn":["Hydrostatic depth alone completely determines bucket pressure","Total hydraulic power alone determines required plunge-pool depth","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; modelV=2 m/s; modelThickness=0.020 m; surfaceTension=0.072 N/m; Weber=1000*2**2*0.020/0.072=1111.11. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b245-v15-39","title":"福祿尺度與表面張力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Froude scaling and surface tension: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「福祿尺度與表面張力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Froude scaling and surface tension” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「福祿尺度與表面張力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Froude scaling and surface tension\"?","options":["比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要流速大小相同沖擊方向也相同"],"optionsEn":["Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal speed guarantees the same direction of impact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b245-v15-40","title":"福祿尺度與表面張力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Froude scaling and surface tension: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b245-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「福祿尺度與表面張力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Froude scaling and surface tension” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「彈道相似就代表破碎與含氣完全相似」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar trajectories guarantee similar breakup and aeration\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b245-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同模型尺度的水舌破碎長度與無因次落點，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare breakup length and dimensionless landing position between model scales. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b245-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「福祿尺度與表面張力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Froude scaling and surface tension\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。","理想中心線落點就是完整水舌沖擊範圍"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration.","The ideal centerline landing point defines the complete jet footprint"],"answer":1,"explanation":"過細模型水舌受表面張力控制會偏離原型含氣機制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An overly thin model jet becomes surface-tension controlled and misrepresents prototype aeration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
